# Device-level patch series.
#
# Empty on purpose since 2026-11-14.
#
# sheng-platform-power.patch used to be listed here. This machine has no Apple PMGR, so AMFI waits for
# an ApplePMGRNub that will never exist and panics with "AMFI: No PMGR?" unless the original PMGR
# provider is invoked at this point in bsd_init(); without the patch the bridge that
# build-platform-power.py compiles is never called and the sheng-pmgr=2 boot argument is a no-op.
#
# The framework this board now builds against (FFT-infra/UniXNU) ships the same patch at the same path
# and its arch series applies it, so listing it here applied the same change twice and the second
# git apply failed at bsd_init.c:688 (run 43555869383). The file stays in this repository: a device
# repository file shadows the framework file at the same path, so keeping it here still controls the
# exact version that gets applied.
#
# The board still lists this series *before* the OS profile's series: the ipados-17.7.11 series'
# zzz-boot-progress.patch edits the same bsd_init() region (it wraps the sheng_pmgr_run() call with
# boot_progress stages) and cannot apply until that block exists.